    "result_text": "The change is complete and the build is green. Here's what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `selfLink` field was specified by the `coreReturnsSelfLink` acceptance test (which does `GET /api/owners/{id}` and asserts `$.selfLink == \"/api/owners/\" + id`) but didn't exist in production code. Two edits implemented it:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `readOnly` `selfLink` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains `getSelfLink`/`setSelfLink`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added one MapStruct mapping on `toOwnerDto(Owner)`:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", expression = \"java(\\\"/api/owners/\\\" + owner.getId())\")\n   ```\n\nWiring it in the mapper (rather than in a single responder) means every owner response \u2014 GET, POST-created, and PUT-updated \u2014 carries a consistent `selfLink`, matching how the other derived DTO fields are handled.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest` passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`) and the full suite reports **BUILD SUCCESS** (the acceptance test is the only test class; the other files in that package are helper base classes).",
